phoenix: qcom_smbx read the AICL-settled ICL status register on SMB5

On PM8150B (SMB5) the DCDC peripheral exposes the input current limit
in two adjacent registers: base+0x07 holds the configured/instantaneous
value (which reads 0 until the charger actively passes current), while
base+0x08 holds the AICL-settled value that userspace expects from
POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_MAX. qcom_smbx reads +0x07 on both
generations, so on phoenix CURRENT_MAX reports 0 whenever charging is
temporarily inhibited even though a 12V USB-PD contract is active.

Select the register offset per generation inside ICL_STATUS(): SMB5
reads base+0x08, SMB2 keeps base+0x07.

Register layout verified against the Xiaomi downstream smb5-reg.h as
documented in postmarketOS soc/qualcomm-sm8150/linux MR 18.

Signed-off-by: phoenix port <fix@me>

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 1d1d041..9fc7531 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -141,7 +141,13 @@ enum smb_generation {
 #define USBIN_CONT_AICL_THRESHOLD_CFG			0x384
 #define USBIN_CONT_AICL_THRESHOLD_CFG_MASK		GENMASK(5, 0)
 
-#define ICL_STATUS(smb)					(SMB_REG_OFFSET(smb) + 0x07)
+/* On SMB5 (PM8150B) the AICL-settled input current limit lives at +0x08;
+ * +0x07 holds the configured/instantaneous value which can read 0.
+ * SMB2 exposes a single ICL status register at +0x07. */
+#define SMB2_ICL_STATUS_REG				0x07
+#define SMB5_ICL_STATUS_REG				0x08
+#define ICL_STATUS(smb)					(SMB_REG_OFFSET(smb) + \
+			((smb)->gen == SMB5 ? SMB5_ICL_STATUS_REG : SMB2_ICL_STATUS_REG))
 #define INPUT_CURRENT_LIMIT_MASK			GENMASK(7, 0)
 
 #define POWER_PATH_STATUS(smb)				(SMB_REG_OFFSET(smb) + 0x0B)
